      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nmG5qLL7ZavWh3Fb_-Q264s5BrOupRVA4K-njIRaAa7A=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "It's funny how Cape Verde is always lauded as this \"beautiful\" country, with \"beautiful\" women while completely negating the historical legacy and reasons as to why Cape Verde is even a country today. The history of that Island is dark, it was nothing more then a sex tourist despot created for rapist and pedophilic Europeans during slavery to bring enslaved African women and little girls to satisfy their personal desires. Yet today, people act as if this history should be ignored because of what the people are today? The amount of mixed children produced as a result of rape, forced marriages, brothels is insanity. The involuntary marriages and forced rapes of young female Africans at the mere age of 13 was abysmal, but this is a country that is a \"jewel\" of Africa?",
      "likeCount": 5,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-06T23:34:09Z",
      "replyCount": 2,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "Ugyi93bfqK8SacADo_54AaABAg.A_BPlv8CZ6WA_UUkTmXnpF",
